    "updated_at": "2016-11-20T02:20:31Z",
    "body": "I see, “list owner” if for numbering. \n\nI though, since browsers allow markup like this, the spec should allow it too.\n\n``` html\n<ul>\n  <li>…</li>\n  <div>\n    <li>…</li>\n  </div>\n  <li>…</li>\n</ul>\n```\n\nBut I guess, this is addressed in the part of the spec that describes how browsers will allow bad markup and try to normalize it, so the above should still be considered invalid.\n",
